Ask one question through the Rust-native Apple M4 CPU/NEON SLM path

Usage: bitnet mac ask [OPTIONS] [QUESTION]

Arguments:
  [QUESTION]  Question to answer. This is the shortest Mac path: `bitnet mac ask "What is 2+2?"`

Options:
  -c, --config <PATH>
          Configuration file path
  -q, --question <QUESTION>
          Question to answer. Kept for scripts that already use `--question`
  -d, --device <DEVICE>
          Device/backend label (cpu, cuda/gpu, hip/rocm, oneapi, npu/openvino-npu, nvidia-rtx-5070-ti-cuda/wgpu, intel-a770-opencl, metal/mpsgraph, apple-m4-metal, apple-m4-mpsgraph, apple-m4-cpu-neon, apple-m3-air-metal, apple-m3-air-mpsgraph, apple-m3-air-cpu-neon, auto). Apple M4 and M3 Air labels are distinct proof lanes
      --model-id <MODEL_ID>
          Supported model id. Defaults to the validated Apple M4 SLM runtime artifact [default: qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-q8_0]
      --cache-dir <PATH>
          Override model cache root. Defaults to ~/.cache/bitnet-rs/models
      --log-level <LEVEL>
          Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
      --model-path <PATH>
          Explicit BitNet GGUF path for the one-shot BitNet ask route
      --batch-size <SIZE>
          Batch size for processing
      --tokenizer <PATH>
          Explicit tokenizer.json path for the one-shot BitNet ask route
      --system <TEXT>
          Optional system prompt
      --max-new-tokens <MAX_NEW_TOKENS>
          Maximum new tokens to generate [default: 32] [aliases: --max-tokens, --n-predict]
      --temperature <TEMPERATURE>
          Temperature for sampling. The Mac wrapper defaults to deterministic greedy [default: 0]
      --top-k <TOP_K>
          Top-k sampling. The Mac wrapper defaults to greedy top-1 behavior [default: 1]
      --top-p <TOP_P>
          Top-p sampling [default: 1]
      --repetition-penalty <REPETITION_PENALTY>
          Repetition penalty [default: 1.1]
      --seed <SEED>
          Random seed for reproducibility
      --threads <THREADS>
          Number of CPU threads to use (0 = all cores; deterministic mode may override) [default: 0]
      --timeout-seconds <SECONDS>
          Optional wall-clock timeout for the explicit BitNet one-shot ask route
      --json-out <PATH>
          Output strict Mac answer receipt [default: target/apple-m4-productization/mac-ask.json]
      --progress
          Emit operator progress lines to stderr while keeping generated text on stdout
      --trace
          Emit redacted trace-correlation diagnostics and record trace IDs in the receipt
      --quiet
          Suppress Mac ask status/progress lines; generated text still uses stdout
  -h, --help
          Print help
